WEBVTT

00:25.970 --> 00:29.710
At last, we see it in its completion.

00:33.020 --> 00:36.040
The Eight Sounds amplification
device, Octovas.

00:36.040 --> 00:37.720
Now we just wait for it to be powered on.

00:38.320 --> 00:39.320
What do you think?

00:43.110 --> 00:43.930
Victory?

00:44.620 --> 00:47.560
As in, "Yay, I love it"?

00:48.320 --> 00:49.760
Two hours.

00:51.040 --> 00:53.780
We power on the Octovas in two hours.

00:53.780 --> 00:55.570
Prepare for it immediately.

00:56.260 --> 00:59.150
Gather all of the ClassicaLoids.

01:00.800 --> 01:02.300
Bach-sama spoke Japanese!

01:02.300 --> 01:03.270
Yeah.

01:03.270 --> 01:04.640
You heard him.

01:04.640 --> 01:06.300
Dispatch recovery squads immediately.

01:06.300 --> 01:06.830
Sir.

01:07.960 --> 01:10.320
Where are Tchaikovsky and Bądarzewska?

01:10.320 --> 01:12.710
They're at photo shoots for idol magazines.

01:13.320 --> 01:16.100
Notify them to come to
my room when they return.

01:16.100 --> 01:17.350
Understood.

01:20.130 --> 01:22.350
You must have wondered

01:23.550 --> 01:27.010
why you're working in show business.

01:27.690 --> 01:29.690
Everything was for this moment.

01:29.950 --> 01:34.400
To know the world as it is today, and
to know the audience of our music.

01:35.090 --> 01:38.990
Everything was in preparation for today.

01:39.300 --> 01:43.510
B-B-Bach-sama's finally
talking to us in Japanese!

01:44.540 --> 01:46.120
What changed?

01:46.300 --> 01:48.300
A world where music exists not as a tool

01:48.300 --> 01:51.790
or as a means to an end,
but purely as its own end.

01:52.330 --> 01:55.510
The device that will make that
a reality has been completed.

01:55.760 --> 01:57.400
Device?

01:57.400 --> 02:00.760
The device will amplify the Eight Sounds:

02:01.070 --> 02:05.770
the pinnacle of Musik, created
by eight ClassicaLoids.

02:07.930 --> 02:09.860
The Eight Sounds.

02:09.860 --> 02:11.600
Eight Sounds?

02:12.820 --> 02:14.980
So that includes us, too?

02:15.490 --> 02:18.990
You, too, are each a note in the
scale that creates the world.

02:19.640 --> 02:21.990
The time is near.

02:22.630 --> 02:25.990
The eight ClassicaLoids will soon gather here.

04:02.840 --> 04:08.560
23: The World of Eight Sounds: Part 1

04:04.030 --> 04:06.510
That was splendid, as always, Liszt-chan.

04:06.510 --> 04:08.920
Your pay will be in your bank account.

04:08.920 --> 04:09.970
Thank you.

04:12.200 --> 04:13.600
Who are you?

04:13.870 --> 04:17.110
ClassicaLoid Liszt, you're coming with us.

04:17.480 --> 04:18.420
What?

04:24.120 --> 04:25.820
ClassicaLoid Mozart.

04:26.570 --> 04:27.510
You're co—

04:28.740 --> 04:31.000
You're coming with us.

04:37.930 --> 04:39.090
Now!

04:43.220 --> 04:44.170
Classica—

04:47.750 --> 04:49.470
Yeah, yeah.

04:49.690 --> 04:52.180
Shopping district's closed, nothing to buy.

04:52.180 --> 04:54.970
Oh by the way, I'm a nice guy.

04:56.110 --> 04:56.730
No.

04:56.990 --> 04:58.030
That should be...

04:58.480 --> 05:01.070
My favorite food is scallop fry.

05:01.070 --> 05:02.430
I guess?

05:03.020 --> 05:04.110
No, but wait...

05:05.470 --> 05:07.200
ClassicaLoid Schubert.

05:07.200 --> 05:08.450
You're coming with us.

05:08.670 --> 05:09.750
I know!

05:10.310 --> 05:13.200
Men in black, OMG why?

05:15.470 --> 05:19.210
Delivery from online shopping for Chopin-san.

05:19.210 --> 05:20.420
Coming.

05:23.310 --> 05:25.000
ClassicaLoid Chopin, correct?

05:25.000 --> 05:26.180
We need to talk.

05:26.340 --> 05:28.400
Don't touch me!

05:49.530 --> 05:51.030
Avocado
Freedom
On my own terms
Self-indulgent
Big mouth
Shopping district
Men in black
OMG why

05:51.030 --> 05:53.890
Shopping district, nothing to buy,

05:53.890 --> 05:55.910
scallop fry, gargle when you get home, guy...

05:57.080 --> 05:58.300
So weak.

05:58.300 --> 06:00.610
What were these guys trying to do?

06:02.330 --> 06:03.460
Failed?

06:03.780 --> 06:04.710
Yes.

06:04.710 --> 06:07.700
They were all shut down with Musik.

06:07.700 --> 06:11.720
I instructed you to take plenty of
precautions against their Musik.

06:12.070 --> 06:14.600
They sure are useless.

06:14.600 --> 06:16.810
But it's nothing I didn't expect.

06:17.470 --> 06:18.930
What do you mean by that?

06:18.930 --> 06:22.190
For better or worse, they're geniuses.

06:22.750 --> 06:25.500
Not only do they have the
supernatural power we call Musik,

06:25.500 --> 06:27.100
but they're also unpredictable and weird.

06:27.100 --> 06:28.240
They lack common sense.

06:28.660 --> 06:31.440
They're too much for us
mere mortals to handle.

06:31.440 --> 06:33.750
Even if we managed to bring them here,

06:33.750 --> 06:36.110
they would start moaning and complaining.

06:36.110 --> 06:38.710
I highly doubt they would be cooperative.

06:39.290 --> 06:44.120
Knowing this, I made some preparations.

06:45.520 --> 06:49.840
These entities are far more obedient
and far more capable than them.

06:52.850 --> 06:54.510
Allow me to introduce...

06:55.050 --> 06:58.230
The seven super-androids,

06:58.230 --> 07:03.230
equipped with artificial intelligence
software evolved from ArkheDol.

07:03.950 --> 07:06.400
I call them MitsuruLoid 2.0.

07:07.360 --> 07:09.620
Obedient and capable?

07:09.620 --> 07:12.110
Beethoven 2.0, show them.

07:12.110 --> 07:12.740
Sir.

07:13.920 --> 07:18.750
Spielen wir unsere Musik!

07:22.190 --> 07:23.250
Musik.

07:24.280 --> 07:29.340
I collected data on their
Musik during past encounters.

07:29.770 --> 07:33.340
We need the Musik of eight
people to start up the Octovas.

07:33.810 --> 07:36.150
Unlike the unstable originals,

07:36.150 --> 07:38.330
they have perfect control of their Musik,

07:38.330 --> 07:40.020
and they're absolutely obedient.

07:40.310 --> 07:44.880
MitsuruLoid 2.0 will bring your
noble ideals to fruition, Bach-sama.

07:52.640 --> 07:55.440
Hey, did Bach-sama go to the research lab?

07:55.440 --> 07:57.740
Should we move, too?

07:58.750 --> 08:00.440
Don't worry about it.

08:01.160 --> 08:04.940
I found way better replacements for you.

08:04.940 --> 08:07.000
You're free to go.

08:07.300 --> 08:08.650
Replacements?

08:08.650 --> 08:09.920
Do you mean...

08:12.930 --> 08:14.510
It looks like you understand.

08:14.820 --> 08:18.250
Honestly, I'm done with you.

08:18.250 --> 08:20.930
Go wherever you'd like.

08:30.920 --> 08:33.780
The hell do you mean, you're "done with us"?

08:33.780 --> 08:35.380
Fired again?

08:35.380 --> 08:38.700
Bach-sama said he needed us.

08:38.700 --> 08:41.200
That woman's up to something again.

08:41.940 --> 08:45.880
She told us to do whatever
we'd like, but where do we go?

08:45.880 --> 08:48.290
Seriously, what do we do now?

08:49.850 --> 08:53.220
What, so we were all attacked?

08:53.220 --> 08:56.140
The fish got away because of them.

08:56.390 --> 08:58.600
You've never caught one, Lud-kun.

08:58.600 --> 08:59.840
Silence!

08:59.840 --> 09:02.290
I could feel a catch coming today.

09:02.290 --> 09:06.380
In fact, I almost caught a tuna that
must have been ten meters long.

09:06.380 --> 09:08.610
I don't even know where to begin.

09:08.990 --> 09:10.360
They attacked you, too, Motes?

09:11.310 --> 09:12.680
They told me to come with them.

09:12.680 --> 09:14.700
It's been a while, huh?

09:15.050 --> 09:18.110
Oh yeah, they came here once before.

09:18.110 --> 09:20.550
They wanted the ClassicaLoids
back or something.

09:20.550 --> 09:22.330
<i>Who</i> wants you back?

09:22.570 --> 09:24.710
Bach, obviously.

09:24.710 --> 09:26.510
Cho-chan and I were originally ordered here

09:26.510 --> 09:30.000
to take Beethes and Motes back, after all.

09:30.810 --> 09:32.040
Really?

09:32.040 --> 09:33.260
Huh.

09:34.800 --> 09:38.550
He's been quiet lately, so
I thought he'd changed his mind.

09:38.830 --> 09:43.340
What does Bach-san want
from the ClassicaLoids?

09:43.340 --> 09:44.280
I don't know.

09:44.870 --> 09:46.370
The Eight Sounds.

09:46.810 --> 09:47.920
Tchaiko-chan.

09:47.920 --> 09:49.470
Bąda-kyun!

09:49.470 --> 09:51.820
We're going to be here for a while.

09:52.310 --> 09:53.700
What's the matter, you two?

09:53.700 --> 09:54.990
Did you get fired again?

09:54.990 --> 09:56.550
Not just us.

09:56.550 --> 09:58.430
You're all fired.

09:58.430 --> 09:59.370
Huh?

09:59.370 --> 10:00.720
What are you talking about?

10:03.410 --> 10:04.720
The Eight Sounds?

10:05.700 --> 10:06.580
So...

10:07.260 --> 10:11.110
In other words, Bach-san
needs eight ClassicaLoids

10:11.110 --> 10:14.090
in order to create his ideal world?

10:14.330 --> 10:16.180
That's what Bach-sama said.

10:16.180 --> 10:17.330
Damn.

10:17.330 --> 10:18.870
Eight people creating a world?

10:18.870 --> 10:20.010
That sounds bad ass.

10:21.700 --> 10:24.900
I've never been able to figure
out what he's thinking.

10:24.900 --> 10:26.640
So that's what he was up to.

10:27.760 --> 10:29.140
I don't like it.

10:29.140 --> 10:32.640
Why am I among a group that
he created by himself?

10:32.640 --> 10:35.490
He's done with you.
You aren't a member anymore.

10:35.490 --> 10:37.280
I don't like that, either.

10:37.600 --> 10:39.310
But why?

10:39.310 --> 10:42.410
He needs the ClassicaLoids
for that project, right?

10:42.780 --> 10:45.250
He found replacements, supposedly.

10:45.250 --> 10:49.990
We saw seven robot things walk
by that look just like us.

10:50.520 --> 10:51.580
Robots?

10:52.120 --> 10:55.250
So those knock-off robots are
going to make a new world?

11:05.890 --> 11:08.390
So we're free to do whatever we want, right?

11:08.390 --> 11:09.700
That's what it means.

11:09.700 --> 11:11.160
I'm going back to fishing.

11:11.160 --> 11:12.930
I'mma go hit on chicks.

11:12.930 --> 11:14.420
Back to my game.

11:14.420 --> 11:15.870
Time for some booze.

11:15.870 --> 11:17.150
I want to watch TV.

11:17.410 --> 11:19.050
Wait, guys.

11:19.050 --> 11:23.460
There's a new world about to
be made or something, right?

11:23.460 --> 11:25.140
Are we just going to let that happen?

11:25.140 --> 11:27.120
It's not our problem.

11:27.340 --> 11:28.390
Oh, man.

11:28.390 --> 11:31.950
What if it's a world where I'm
the most popular guy ever?

11:31.950 --> 11:35.240
I'm sure you'll live a long
life in any world, Sousuke.

11:35.240 --> 11:36.750
Really?

12:06.140 --> 12:08.620
All right, I'm going to start up the Octovas.

12:08.950 --> 12:10.970
We're going to use Bach-sama's Musik

12:10.970 --> 12:13.960
as a base to amplify the other seven's Musik.

12:14.850 --> 12:17.710
Bach-sama, your Musik, please.

12:34.710 --> 12:36.690
Octovas initialized.

12:48.230 --> 12:50.870
Alpha to Eta values above threshold.

12:57.550 --> 12:58.740
Hatch opening.

13:00.570 --> 13:02.340
Entering Phase Two.

13:04.770 --> 13:06.450
Speakers all green.

13:07.380 --> 13:09.380
Brilliant.

13:09.380 --> 13:11.720
The world's going to be reborn.

13:11.720 --> 13:13.940
Musik energy continuing to rise.

13:13.940 --> 13:14.840
We're good.

13:14.840 --> 13:16.650
Octovas Alpha away.

13:59.190 --> 14:02.690
Mysterious Events All Across Japan

14:02.690 --> 14:04.190
Please stand by

14:04.190 --> 14:05.220
Huh?

14:05.690 --> 14:08.880
Weird, I can't hear anything.

14:08.880 --> 14:11.070
Try smacking it.

14:22.990 --> 14:25.210
What are you doing, Sousuke?

14:31.850 --> 14:35.720
My voice is gone!!

14:32.680 --> 14:33.980
Are you sick?

14:36.420 --> 14:38.310
What are you two doing?

14:38.520 --> 14:40.690
If you have something to say, then say it.

14:41.270 --> 14:43.650
I told you, we can't talk.

14:44.720 --> 14:49.410
I lost sound in my game, and a
monster attacked me, and I died.

14:49.410 --> 14:53.200
It took me so long to get up to level 200.

14:56.340 --> 14:58.180
Huh? It didn't make a sound.

14:58.180 --> 14:59.680
What's going on?

14:59.680 --> 15:02.250
My little kitten and the
tool can't speak, either.

15:02.600 --> 15:04.080
No good here, either.

15:04.080 --> 15:06.510
Every channel is having audio problems.

15:06.710 --> 15:12.340
I can't send voice messages, either.

15:10.100 --> 15:12.340
Is that you talking, Pad-kun?

15:12.720 --> 15:13.600
Yes.

15:13.600 --> 15:15.850
My mic array sensor isn't picking
up anything at all, either.

15:15.850 --> 15:18.350
It seems that sound itself
has suddenly vanished.

15:18.830 --> 15:20.610
Sound has vanished?

15:20.610 --> 15:22.380
How could that happen?

15:24.270 --> 15:26.900
How come you guys can still talk?!

15:28.550 --> 15:29.470
Dunno.

15:36.080 --> 15:37.410
What's going on?

15:37.410 --> 15:38.500
I don't know!

15:38.500 --> 15:39.910
What? I can't hear anything.

15:39.910 --> 15:41.420
I can't hear you, either!

15:41.860 --> 15:43.460
What on Earth...

15:44.060 --> 15:45.380
What's going on?

15:49.760 --> 15:51.010
Dude, you can talk?!

15:51.010 --> 15:52.970
How come you can talk?!

15:52.970 --> 15:54.510
Is this your fault?!

15:56.300 --> 15:57.910
No, wait...

15:58.810 --> 16:01.100
So the ClassicaLoids aren't affected?

16:01.540 --> 16:03.330
Looks like it.

16:03.330 --> 16:04.790
But why?

16:04.790 --> 16:08.190
It must be because of the
device Bach-sama made.

16:08.560 --> 16:12.570
So this is the world that
Bach wanted to make?

16:12.820 --> 16:14.910
A world without sound?

16:27.440 --> 16:31.240
A ray of light in a world of chaos.

16:31.240 --> 16:33.130
This is truly a divine revelation.

16:33.960 --> 16:35.320
Octovas Beta.

16:35.320 --> 16:36.050
Go!

16:42.630 --> 16:43.350
What?

16:43.710 --> 16:45.010
I can hear.

16:47.910 --> 16:49.210
Music?

16:50.190 --> 16:51.920
It's really nice.

16:52.580 --> 16:53.620
What...

16:56.000 --> 16:57.870
Is this Musik?

16:57.870 --> 16:58.850
Really?

16:59.320 --> 17:00.370
Hey, I can talk.

17:00.640 --> 17:01.890
Isn't this piece...

17:01.890 --> 17:05.750
The first movement of the
unaccompanied Cello Suite No. 1

17:05.750 --> 17:08.130
by Johann Sebastian Bach, "Prelude."

17:08.380 --> 17:09.850
By Bach-sama?

17:13.870 --> 17:15.510
Where'd you get that wig?

17:16.030 --> 17:17.340
Grave.

17:17.810 --> 17:19.150
Andantino.

17:19.150 --> 17:20.470
Uh...

17:20.470 --> 17:21.940
Pianissimo.

17:24.290 --> 17:25.780
Da capo.

17:26.160 --> 17:27.860
Dal segno.

17:28.180 --> 17:29.850
Sostenuto.

17:29.850 --> 17:30.880
Ritardando.

17:30.880 --> 17:32.280
Staccato.

17:32.280 --> 17:34.170
Fermata.

17:37.410 --> 17:38.120
Fermata.

17:38.120 --> 17:39.410
Andante.

17:42.290 --> 17:43.330
Meow.

17:46.430 --> 17:48.640
Bach's wigs here, there, everywhere!

17:48.640 --> 17:50.960
What is with this peculiar air?

17:50.960 --> 17:55.720
Mass Outbreak of J. S. Bach?!

17:51.380 --> 17:53.070
Can you see this?

17:53.070 --> 17:55.720
People all across town are Bachifying.

17:55.720 --> 18:00.000
It's the very sight of the father of music,
the man of the famous portrait, Bach.

18:00.000 --> 18:03.990
It appears that it's being caused by the
Bach music that's been playing since earlier.

18:01.650 --> 18:03.020
What the heck?

18:03.020 --> 18:08.940
Mass Outbreak of J. S. Bach?!

18:03.990 --> 18:05.160
Details remain...

18:07.370 --> 18:08.940
Crescendo.

18:10.020 --> 18:12.270
It's Bach-sama everywhere.

18:12.270 --> 18:14.490
This is the new world?

18:41.600 --> 18:42.810
Bach-sama.

18:42.810 --> 18:44.110
Are you awake?

18:44.110 --> 18:45.610
What do you think you're doing?

18:46.960 --> 18:48.640
This is my music.

18:49.110 --> 18:50.690
What's going on?

18:50.690 --> 18:54.480
The Eight Sounds are to be created
together from eight Musiks.

18:54.780 --> 18:56.590
It's noise.

18:56.590 --> 18:57.730
Noise?

18:57.730 --> 19:01.950
Anything that isn't by the
great Bach-sama is just noise.

19:03.300 --> 19:07.200
I've been thinking, ever
since I met your greatness,

19:07.460 --> 19:11.710
that we only need your music in the new world.

19:11.710 --> 19:15.310
We don't need those small
fry, Beethoven and Mozart.

19:15.310 --> 19:20.170
A new world created from the Musik of
Eight Sounds created by Eight Bach-samas.

19:20.170 --> 19:24.340
A truly ideal world is one where
all humanity becomes Bach-sama.

19:24.840 --> 19:25.970
I'm so moved.

19:25.970 --> 19:27.730
I can't sit still.

19:27.730 --> 19:32.700
The fact your ideal is brought to life
not by Professor Otowa's ClassicaLoids,

19:32.700 --> 19:35.730
but by my own creations, the MitsuruLoids...

19:36.160 --> 19:38.380
The world is about to change.

19:38.380 --> 19:41.880
And you're going to become the eternal god

19:41.880 --> 19:44.450
at the center of the new world, Bach-sama.

19:45.080 --> 19:46.160
Mitsuru.

19:46.670 --> 19:47.800
You...

19:50.060 --> 19:51.330
Bach-sama...

19:51.730 --> 19:54.590
You said my name for the first time.

19:58.330 --> 20:03.080
Watch me color the whole
world with your music.

20:08.760 --> 20:09.730
Here we go.

20:10.690 --> 20:13.150
Looks like they started up that device.

20:13.990 --> 20:17.890
Good thing I set up a back door.

20:18.820 --> 20:21.780
We can't have them changing
the world all by themselves.

20:21.780 --> 20:23.610
Sorry, but I'm going to have to stop you.

20:26.900 --> 20:27.570
Huh?

20:29.950 --> 20:31.750
Uh, Landlord?

20:31.750 --> 20:33.500
My power just went out.

20:33.750 --> 20:34.920
I don't know anything about it.

20:35.130 --> 20:36.880
It's because you don't pay your power bill!

20:37.040 --> 20:38.210
No, but...

20:38.210 --> 20:40.090
I need power. It's really important.

20:40.090 --> 20:41.760
Take your complaints to the power company!

20:43.960 --> 20:45.840
What now?

20:50.330 --> 20:51.500
This is bad.

20:51.910 --> 20:53.420
There's even more of them.

20:55.440 --> 20:56.030
Allegro.

20:56.030 --> 20:56.610
No!

20:56.610 --> 20:57.800
Sousuke!

20:56.610 --> 20:57.800
Allegretto.

20:57.800 --> 20:59.230
Get a grip, tool!

20:59.230 --> 21:00.920
Don't let him control you!

21:03.620 --> 21:04.860
What did I...

21:05.290 --> 21:07.820
Thank goodness, you're back.

21:08.830 --> 21:10.390
Sforzando.

21:10.390 --> 21:12.300
Kanae, come back!

21:14.030 --> 21:15.630
What happened to me?

21:15.630 --> 21:18.550
You have to stay strong, or the
Musik is going to take you.

21:18.550 --> 21:20.440
Diminuendo.

21:23.750 --> 21:25.150
There's no end to it.

21:26.820 --> 21:28.020
Largo.

21:28.020 --> 21:29.930
Mezzo forte.

21:28.390 --> 21:29.930
Damn pests.

21:30.170 --> 21:33.380
I'll set you all straight with my Musik!

21:44.540 --> 21:45.840
What happened?

21:45.840 --> 21:47.320
What on Earth?

21:50.480 --> 21:51.580
Piece of cake.

21:51.580 --> 21:52.900
Of course.

22:00.490 --> 22:02.210
There's still so many.

22:02.520 --> 22:04.070
We can handle them.

22:04.070 --> 22:07.850
We have seven people who can use Musik.

22:07.850 --> 22:08.750
Right.

22:10.950 --> 22:12.850
One, two,

22:12.850 --> 22:15.230
three, four,

22:15.230 --> 22:17.320
five, six...

22:18.040 --> 22:18.610
Huh?

22:19.700 --> 22:21.330
Shouldn't there be one more?

22:21.330 --> 22:22.410
You're right.

22:26.360 --> 22:27.660
Moderato.

22:28.690 --> 22:29.810
Fine.

22:30.990 --> 22:33.990
To be continued

24:03.960 --> 24:08.300
The greatest scourge in existence: the
amalgamation of idealism and passion.

24:03.960 --> 24:24.480
The World of Eight Sounds: Part 2

24:08.300 --> 24:13.180
The more intertwined and rigid they are,
the purer and more glowing it becomes.

24:13.180 --> 24:17.470
Oh, source of all turmoil,
fountain of tragedy.

24:17.460 --> 24:18.600
I'll be clear:

24:18.610 --> 24:24.480
The forceful pursuit of perfection
is the bane of humanity.

24:24.480 --> 24:26.510
I'll say it again, if you still don't get it.

24:26.510 --> 24:27.520
Leave me alone!

24:27.520 --> 24:29.300
Let me be!
